Follow-up to k300 (2026-10-31). Since k300, `OCP::Cmd::Apply::Network::setup_cilium_gateway` returns 'deployed', 'updated' or 'unchanged' and prints the matching line. The reconcile caller in lib/OCP/Cmd/Apply/Drift.pm (around line 385) ignores that and always prints `[ok] Cilium Gateway up to date`, even after it created or updated the Gateway, and the run's update count misses it.

Fix proposed by the k300 worker (one line, keep the STDERR else-branch):
    eval { $updated += $self->_report_component('Cilium Gateway', $self->_setup_cilium_gateway($config)); 1 }
Check that `_report_component` prints the `[ok]` line in the house wording for each outcome and that `$updated` is the counter the run summary uses.

Done = the [ok] line and the update count follow the outcome; a test pins all three. Waits for k291 (Apply/Drift.pm is in that change).

